  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Understand why A. oryzae assimilates lactate poorly and find conditions that improve it, to valorise lactate-rich food by-products.",
    "experimental_design": "RIB40 was grown at 30 °C in modified Czapek-Dox minimal medium with glucose (48 h), lactate as sole carbon source (96 h) or lactate plus 0.1% glucose (days 1, 3 and 5; the paper analyses day 3); 3 replicates each.",
    "main_finding": "On lactate alone growth and uptake were minimal and expression pointed to limited carbon flux into the TCA cycle; small amounts of sugars, specific amino acids or α-ketoglutarate, plus low pH, made lactate assimilation efficient."
  },
